<title>UK: SBC unit ups 10-yr bond to 500 mln marks.</title>
<headline>SBC unit ups 10-yr bond to 500 mln marks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated bond has been increased to 500 million marks from 400 million marks, lead manager SBC Warburg ssid on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The new paper was reoffered at 99.88.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWISS BANK CORP, JERSEY BRANCH</p>
<p> AMT    500 MLN DEM   COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    06.DEC.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.98    PAY DATE    06.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	REOFFER   *98.88     SPREAD	+60 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *ORIGINAL 400 MLN DEM REOFFERED AT 98.97.</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    FFT LON   GOV LAW     ENG/SWISS</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS ***</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.40	SELL CONC  2.10	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES   ***US/UK/DE/CHANNEL ISLANDS. ISSUED OFF MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
